eval_note:
Evaluate both readouts with --loudness_norm --loudness_norm_lufs -23 (read from config.yaml): the top-5 merge, which is the objective, and epoch_8. Checkpoints are plain ModelSLS state_dicts.

Compare against B3a-top5 / B3a-ep8 (the current best) and the fixed comparators B2f-top5 / B2f-ep8, with the paired-bootstrap CI at n 2000.

Report:
- mean noisy EER and the full-set SNR-0 EER;
- the half_B noisy bona share at p >= 0.99 / 0.999 and the number of false alarms, split en / zh;
- per-set R_bona / R_spoof;
- the best global logit threshold;
- per-epoch CE, JS and the JS share of train_loss from metrics.jsonl (lambda is now 1.0, so train_loss = CE + 1.0*JS), compared with B3a's.

This run isolates the divergence weight from B3a's step / view confound. State explicitly which side of falsifier 1 it lands on.

header_text:
B3c = B3a with one flag changed: --consistency_lambda 1.0, up from 0.3. This is the JS consistency dose step. Everything else is identical to B3a:
- --consistency js --consistency_pairs both;
- --batch_size 8 = 8 pairs = 16 clips/step;
- 8 epochs, LR 2.5e-6 warmup-cosine to 5e-7, the same 75792 steps;
- sampler shuffle, CE weights 0.1 0.9;
- RTC aug + MUSAN, loudness norm -23.
It runs ~8 h.

Evidence:
- B3a, consistency at lambda 0.3, is the only above-band gain of the wave: merge half_B 93.06 against B2f 91.98, noisy EER 10.09 -> 9.16. Its JS term was only 2.5-4.5 % of the train loss (B3a metrics.jsonl), and the report could not tell whether the gain came from the divergence weight or from the doubled steps / two views.
- B3b, the balanced sampler, was negative at -0.83 [-1.46, -0.25]. It ruled out exposure and the operating point as the cause of the residual error.

Target: confident noisy bona false alarms, a ranking error. On the B3a merge, 180 of 782 half_B noisy bona are false alarms, 77 % of them at p_spoof >= 0.99, and English carries 91 of the 180.

Rule against B3a-top5 = 93.06 on half_B: promote if the delta is > +0.5, the CI excludes 0 and the clean drop is <= 0.5; null within +-0.5; negative below -0.5. A null delta with noisy EER within +-0.3 of 9.16 means the JS weight is not the active ingredient (keep 0.3).
